# Build output.
#
# These are anchored with a leading slash on purpose. A bare "openconsole"
# matches at any depth, which silently swallowed cmd/openconsole/ and
# cmd/openconsole-server/ — the two entry points — so a clone of this
# repository had no main packages and could not be built at all.
/bin/
/dist/
/openconsole
/openconsole-server

# Web toolchain. internal/webui/dist is generated but IS committed, so that
# `go build` produces a relay with a working UI and no Node toolchain. Rebuild
# it with `npm --prefix web run build` after changing anything under web/src.
web/node_modules/
web/.vite/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
# Also the project brief, which lives here under the same name and is not
# something the repository needs to carry.
.idea
.idea/

# Go
*.test
*.out
